{"excerpt": "[7f10319ed7f3] (school: school-2)\nCLAIM: A token bucket that refills request tokens and byte tokens at configurable rates provides a flexible, burst-tolerant budget; exhaustion is recorded as a typed terminal when the bucket is empty and a fetch cannot be satisfied, with the bucket level history for audit.\nMECHANISM: The agent maintains two token buckets: one for requests (capacity C_r, refill rate R_r requests per second) and one for bytes (capacity C_b, refill rate R_b bytes per second). Before a fetch, the agent attempts to consume 1 request token and estimated_bytes byte tokens. If either bucket has insufficient tokens, the fetch is denied and exhaustion is recorded with reason 'token_bucket_exhausted', along with the current token counts and the refill schedule. The refill is based on a deterministic simulated clock that advances with each fetch or wall-clock time, ensuring reproduc", "handle": "ART_17", "kind": "formal_artifact"}
